  `audio-release` (one occurrence each), proving the converted module
  reached the output.
- App launched via `npx electron --no-sandbox .` with a temporary probe
  appended to `build/main/index.js` (never to source), reaching
  `init: 627.986ms`. The probe read the DOM: `.header` present (463
  chars, identical to the US-006 anchor) and `.torrent-list` rendered
  11 `.torrent` rows with real names. The only severity-3 renderer
  console line is the pre-existing `electron.remote` /
  `getCurrentWindow` failure recorded under US-005. `npm run build` was
  re-run afterwards and `build/main/index.js` confirmed clean.
- The six-step manual smoke test was **not** run -- this session is
  non-interactive. The player page specifically was NOT exercised at
  runtime: a second read-only probe over `state.saved.torrents` found
  no torrent with a downloaded media file, so there was nothing to open
  without starting a real download. Opening a video, play/pause and
  seek therefore carry the residual risk for this story; the evidence
  for `player-page.js` is static (lint, Babel compile, Vite bundle
  inclusion) plus the fact that `app.js` resolves it as a default
  export at startup alongside the torrent list.

**Learnings for future iterations:**

- **`state.saved.torrents` is not a probe fixture for playback.** On a
  fresh-ish install the entries carry no populated `files` array with
  local media, so `dispatch('playFile', ...)` has nothing to open.
  Any story whose acceptance criteria mention playback needs either a
  seeded fixture torrent committed for the purpose or an honest "not
  verified at runtime" note. Do not invent a download to satisfy it.
- **Appending a second probe block without rebuilding stacks them.**
  `build/` is not cleaned between `cat >>` calls, so the previous
  probe still fires and its output interleaves with the new one. Run
  `npm run build` between probes, not just at the end.
- **`.torrent-list` row count is a usable stable anchor** (11 rows
  here) even though the per-row progress text drifts run to run. Count
  rows and read `.name`; do not diff the list's outerHTML.
