  (CANCEL/REMOVE). `dispatch('exitModal')` then removed `.modal`.
- A second probe covered the non-modal components: the preferences page
  rendered 5 `Heading`s (Folders, Playback, Default torrent app,
  General, Trackers) and 3 `PathSelector`s (three CHANGE buttons), and
  `dispatch('showCreateTorrent', ['/tmp/wt-probe8'])` rendered "Create
  torrent wt-probe8 / 2 files, 3 B / Path:/tmp/wt-probe8/ / SHOW
  ADVANCED SETTINGS... / CANCEL / CREATE TORRENT", the last of which is
  `ShowMore`. `header` is proven by `.header` being present at load.
- The only severity-3 renderer console line is the pre-existing
  `electron.remote` /`getCurrentWindow` failure recorded under US-005,
  plus a pre-existing Material-UI "provide an id or a name" TextField
  warning on the preferences page. Neither is new.
- `npm run build` was re-run afterwards; `build/main/index.js` is clean
  (0 `PROBE` matches) and no electron process is left running.
- The six-step manual smoke test was **not** run -- this session is
  non-interactive. Residual risk: 10 of the 11 components were rendered
  and read back, but only *rendered*, not clicked. The OK/Cancel
  handlers (actually removing a torrent, opening VLC, clicking CHANGE
  to open a native dialog) were not exercised. `create-torrent-error-
  page.js` was not rendered at all -- see below; its evidence is
  static.

**Learnings for future iterations:**

- **Rendering an arbitrary modal non-interactively:** there is no
  dispatch action for most of them, but `update()` runs after every
  dispatch, so `window.state.modal = { id: '<modal-id>', ...props }`
  followed by a harmless `window.dispatch('setTitle',
  window.state.window.title)` renders it. Read
  `document.querySelector('.modal-content').innerText`. The modal ids
  are the keys of the `Modals` map in `pages/app.js`. This is the
  cheapest way to satisfy any "the modals still work" criterion.
- **`dispatch('showCreateTorrent', [dir])` is asynchronous.** It walks
  the folder before navigating, so a read immediately afterwards
  returns the *previous* page and looks like a failure. Wait ~1.5s.
  Same for `dispatch('preferences')` (~800ms). The US-007 note about
  stacking probes has a sibling: unwaited reads are the other way to
  get a convincing but wrong probe result.
- **`components/create-torrent-error-page.js` is dead code.**
  `create-torrent-page.js` returns it from its **constructor**
  (`if (files.length === 0) return (<CreateTorrentErrorPage/>)`), which
  JS treats as replacing the constructed instance, not as a render.
  Pointing `showCreateTorrent` at a directory of only dotfiles renders
  nothing at all. Pre-existing, unrelated to ESM -- do not try to
  "fix" it inside a conversion story, and do not burn a session trying
  to render it.
- **Material-UI colours are the only import shape that changes a use
  site.** Every other conversion in this layer was header-only, but
  `require('material-ui/styles/colors')` binds a namespace, so
  switching to named imports means editing `colors.greyNNN` at each
  use too. Grep for `colors\.` before assuming a file is header-only.
