## 2026-07-28 - US-024
- Implemented `src/renderer/lib/platform/dialog.js` against
  `@electron/remote`'s `dialog` + `getCurrentWindow`:
  `showOpenDialog(options)` resolves to `string[]` (empty on cancel,
  where `showOpenDialogSync` returns `undefined`) and
  `showSaveDialog(options)` resolves to `string|null`. Both parent to
  the current window internally, so no caller passes one.
- Implemented `src/renderer/lib/platform/window.js`: `isVisible()`
  and `isMaximized()`, each resolving the current window per call.
- **Interpretation of the "current-window access" criterion.** The
  criterion reads "covers `isVisible()`, `isMaximized()`, and
  current-window access, all async". I took that to mean `window.js`
  *owns* current-window access, not that it exports a handle. A
  `BrowserWindow` proxy is not serialisable and exporting it would
  put an Electron object back in front of callers, against FR-12 and
  the directory's "nothing here returns a Node object" rule. A test
  asserts the module's export list is exactly the two reads.
- `screen.getAllDisplays()` stays excluded; its absence was already
  recorded in `docs/platform-shim.md` and is unchanged.
- Documented the sync-to-async risk site for US-027: `setDimensions()`
  in `src/renderer/main.js`. The PRD cites lines 443-455; the code is
  at 407-422 today (the US-002 telemetry deletion moved it), and the
  doc says so rather than repeating the stale numbers.
- Files changed: `src/renderer/lib/platform/dialog.js`,
  `src/renderer/lib/platform/window.js`,
  `src/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md`, `test/AGENTS.md`,
  `test/unit/platform-dialog.js` (new),
  `test/unit/platform-window.js` (new), `docs/platform-shim.md`,
  `specs/prd.json`.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `@electron/remote`'s renderer entry sets `__esModule: true` and
    defines each builtin (`dialog`, `clipboard`, ...) as a lazy
    getter on `exports` via `addBuiltinProperty`, with **no
    `default`**. So `import { dialog } from '@electron/remote'` is
    the correct shape inside the shim -- same situation as
    `material-ui/styles/colors`. The `import remote from
    '@electron/remote'` in `path-selector.js`,
    `subtitles-controller.js` and `torrent-list-controller.js` works
    only because Rolldown's CJS-external interop synthesises a
    default; under Babel (which builds `lib/`) that form would be
    `undefined`. Anything moved into `src/renderer/lib/` must use
    named imports.
  - Stubbing `@electron/remote` in a unit test needs
    `__esModule: true` on the seeded `exports`, otherwise Babel's
    interop wraps the stub in a `default` and the named import reads
    `undefined`. `require.resolve('@electron/remote')` is safe: it
    resolves without executing, so the real module's "cannot be
    required in the browser process" throw never fires.
  - The sync-to-async hazard in `setDimensions` is *ordering*, not
    just plumbing: the `window.screenX`/`outerWidth` reads and the
    maximize check currently describe one instant. US-027 must take
    the DOM reads before the first `await` and collapse the two
    `isMaximized()` calls into one.
