  omit.** US-026's criteria name four files; the doc's `readText` row
  also names `main.js:497`. Cross-check the doc's tables against the
  criteria at the start of every remaining migration story, or the
  grep criterion in the same story will fail.
- **The boundary grep belongs in a test, not just in the session.**
  `test/unit/platform-boundary.js` reads `src/` (not `build/`, which
  contains no `components/` or `controllers/`) and is the one place a
  migration regression gets caught. Extend its concern list --
  `['shell', 'clipboard']` today -- as each of US-027..US-032 lands,
  until US-034 replaces it with a lint rule.
- **Probing a modal non-interactively:** `wc.executeJavaScript(
  "window.dispatch('openTorrentAddress')")` opens it and the DOM is
  readable ~1.5s later. Seed OS state (clipboard, etc.) from the main
  process with a plain `require('electron')` in the appended probe
  block -- it does not have to come from the renderer.
