    `userStories`. It already carries the Phase 3, Phase 4 and
    casting decisions (`engineTransport`, `dualHost`, `rustChecks`,
    `manualStories`, `deferredCasualties`) in one or two sentences
    each. An ADR story is therefore expanding a decision that is
    already made and must not contradict it -- read the matching
    `conventions` key before writing the ADR, and read the
    downstream stories (US-038..US-046 here) because their acceptance
    criteria are the ADR's implementation detail and the ADR should
    agree with them exactly (`src/shared/wire.js`, port 0 on stdout,
