## 2026-07-29 - US-045

Delete the hidden window and the wt-* relay.

**What was implemented**

Test first: `test/unit/hidden-window-removed.js`, 25 assertions, red
before the change (16 failures) and green after. Two halves --
a source scan for each piece of the old topology, and a behavioural
check that requires the built `build/main/ipc.js` against stubbed
`electron`/`log`/`menu`/`windows` and asserts `init()` leaves
`ipcMain.emit` alone, so an engine-prefixed event now reaches its own
listener instead of being routed on a window title.

Deleted outright: `static/webtorrent.html`,
`src/main/windows/webtorrent.js`, `src/renderer/webtorrent.js` (434
lines), `src/engine/bus-electron.js` and its test
`test/unit/engine-bus-electron.js`. The one assertion that test carried
and `engine-entry.js` did not -- no subscription bypasses `bus.on` --
was moved into `test/unit/engine-entry.js` rather than dropped.

Edited: `src/main/windows/index.js` (webtorrent export gone),
`src/main/ipc.js` (the `ipcMain.emit` override, the
`messageQueueMainToWebTorrent` queue and the `ipcReadyWebTorrent`
handshake all gone, replaced by a comment saying no engine traffic
passes through the host), `src/main/index.js` (no
`windows.webtorrent.init()`), `src/main/menu.js` (the "Show WebTorrent
Process" devtools item gone), `src/config.js` (`WINDOW_WEBTORRENT`
removed from both export shapes).

**Deviation from AC-6, stated deliberately.** The criterion asks that
no `nodeIntegration`, `enableRemoteModule` or `AudioVideoTracks`
webPreferences remain anywhere in `src/main/`. Only
`enableRemoteModule` could go honestly, and it did -- from `about.js`
and `main.js` as well as with the deleted file; it has been a no-op
since Electron 14, `@electron/remote` is enabled by an explicit
`.enable()` call. The other two are still load-bearing on the two
visible windows: the Vite renderer bundle is CJS and its `require()`
externals only resolve under `nodeIntegration: true` (ADR-004), and
`pages/player-page.js:125` enumerates `mediaElement.audioTracks`, which
needs `enableBlinkFeatures: 'AudioVideoTracks'` (the US-082 casualty).
Deleting either would break the running app, so the test asserts the
`enableRemoteModule` half and documents why the rest waits for Phase 4,
where the Tauri host removes both by construction.

`--ignore` in `build:main` needed no change: it names
`src/renderer/main.js`, `components/`, `controllers/` and `pages/`, all
of which still exist. The new test asserts that rather than asserting
the absence of a particular string, so it keeps holding as the list
changes.

**Files changed**

- deleted: `static/webtorrent.html`, `src/main/windows/webtorrent.js`,
  `src/renderer/webtorrent.js`, `src/engine/bus-electron.js`,
  `test/unit/engine-bus-electron.js`
- `src/main/ipc.js`, `src/main/index.js`, `src/main/menu.js`,
  `src/main/windows/index.js`, `src/main/windows/about.js`,
  `src/main/windows/main.js`, `src/config.js`
- `vite.config.js` (the `crypto` externals comment named the deleted
  file as its only importer; it is `src/engine/index.js` now)
- `test/unit/hidden-window-removed.js` (new),
  `test/unit/engine-entry.js`
- `src/AGENTS.md`, `src/engine/AGENTS.md`, `progress.log`,
  `specs/prd.json`

**Verification**

- `npx tape test/unit/hidden-window-removed.js`: 16 of 25 failing
  before the change, 25/25 after.
- `npm test`: 1700 assertions pass, exit 0 (standard + lint:boundary +
  depcheck + test-unit).
- `npm run build`: both halves clean, 0 externalization warnings.
- Launch check: `init: 818ms`, sidecar up
  (`pgrep -fl "engine/index.js"` matched), no new errors, one window.
  Process tree killed and `pgrep -fl "$PWD/node_modules/"` clean.
- Smoke test NOT run -- non-interactive session. The residual risk is
  concentrated in step 2 onward (add a torrent, play a file): the UI
  has talked only to the sidecar since US-044, so this story removed a
  path nothing was using, but nothing here re-proves that end to end.

**Learnings for future iterations:**

- **Deleting a file leaves its Babel output behind.** `build/` is not
  cleaned by `npm run build`, so `build/engine/bus-electron.js`,
  `build/renderer/webtorrent.js` and `build/main/windows/webtorrent.js`
  all survived the deletion and would have kept loading if anything
  still required them. `rm` the stale artifacts (or `npm run clean`)
  before any launch check that is meant to prove a deletion.
- **Unit-testing `src/main/ipc.js` works.** It destructures
  `electron` at module scope, so seed `require.cache` for `electron`
  (an `EventEmitter` for `ipcMain` and one for `app`) plus
  `build/main/log`, `build/main/menu` and `build/main/windows` before
  the first require, then **restore the previous cache entries rather
  than deleting them** -- the tape process is shared and a
  later-globbed file may be relying on a seed an earlier one placed.
  `init()` only registers handlers, so nothing lazy inside them loads.
- **The eslint-boundary override and the `lint-boundary.js` assertion
  for `src/renderer/webtorrent.js` were left in place on purpose.**
  ESLint does not require an override's file to exist and the test
  lints synthetic text at that path, so both still pass; removing them
  is explicitly US-046's first criterion.
- **An acceptance criterion can be wrong about scope.** AC-6 here would
  have broken the app if taken literally. The honest move is to do the
  part that is real, assert that part in the test, and write down which
  part was refused and why -- not to widen the deletion or to quietly
  skip the criterion.
