    `player-page.js:185-191` dereferences `mediaElement.videoTracks.length`
    and `.audioTracks.length` with no `|| []` guard, unlike line 125.
    On a webview without the flag those throw inside
    `onLoadedMetadata`, killing playback startup, not just the audio
    menu. That is US-081's problem (codec fallback), not only US-082's
    (multi-track casualty), and it has to be fixed by the cutover.
  - **ADR-004 (CJS + host externals) expires at US-072.** It only works
    because the Electron window has `nodeIntegration: true`. The Tauri
    bundle has to be ESM with `electron` and `@electron/remote` out of
    the external list; there is no `require` to resolve them.
  - **`package.json`'s `engines` field is stale** -- `^16 || ^18`, while
    Vite 8 needs Node 20.19+. Left alone here because the story forbids
    code changes; worth folding into a Phase 4 story that touches
    `package.json` anyway.
