  US-063 also claims. Taken here as `win.setProgressBar` -- the
  window's own taskbar bar. `setBadge` and the rest of
  `src/main/dock.js` stay stubbed for US-063.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - **Tauri's `set_size` sizes the *content* area**, so Electron's
    `setContentBounds` is the free case and its plain `setBounds` is
    the one needing work: subtract `outer_size - inner_size` or the
    window grows by a title bar every time a saved rectangle is
    restored. (`restore()` in `main.rs` still passes the saved *outer*
    rectangle to `set_size`; the drift is a title bar per restore and
    is worth revisiting.)
  - **Tauri 2 has no aspect-ratio API and no fullscreen event.** The
    first is a documented casualty (macOS player edge-drag no longer
    snaps); the second is recoverable, because entering fullscreen
    arrives as an ordinary `Resized` -- read `is_fullscreen()` there
    and edge-detect, which also catches a fullscreen entered from the
